/T (stopping and terminating are the same, there is a difference. When you stop an EC2 instance, it performs a normal shutdown on the instance and moves to a stopped state. However, when you terminate the instance, it is moved to a stopped state and the EBS volumes attached to it are deleted and can never be recovered. )
/E (stopping and terminating are the same, there is a difference. When you stop an EC2 instance, it performs a normal shutdown on the instance and moves to a stopped state. However, when you terminate the instance, it is moved to a stopped state and the EBS volumes attached to it are deleted and can never be recovered. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [13]
>>
